{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqxyjeuq541","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","summary":"The isolated bench daemon sets ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS=0 (bench/zonoid_bench/daemon.py:293), so the headless judge drain never runs. Consequence: ANY judge-mediated memory feature is inert in the bench — contradiction supersession (task #8), autowire context-edge keep/prune, and dup-cluster consolidation all require the judge, which is off. Observed live on the warm ls20 run: eagerJudge queue = 69 items, judgedClusters = 0, zero verdicts, zero superseded notes; the gated contradiction-supersession (ZONOID_CONTRADICTION_RESOLUTION=1) detected/queued but could never adjudicate. Why drains are off in bench: the drain spawns claude -p judge subprocesses that would perturb the controlled single-agent measurement and burn extra usage. Implication: to validate judge-mediated features, run them where drains are ON (main daemon) OR run a one-shot judge drain against the bench daemon after the run OR add a judge-on bench variant. SEPARATE design point surfaced same run: contradiction supersession is correct for a stale-vs-current FACT (marker moved) but WRONG for competing UNVERIFIED hypotheses (ls20 avatar-dock vs top-box win theory, neither scored) — auto-superseding could retire the correct one; keep both until evidence (a score) decides.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-28T19:13:04.167Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqxyjeuq541","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Bench daemon disables judge drains so judge mediated memory features cannot validate there","summary":"The isolated bench daemon sets ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS=0 (bench/zonoid_bench/daemon.py:293), so the headless judge drain never runs. Consequence: ANY judge-mediated memory feature is inert in the bench — contradiction supersession (task #8), autowire context-edge keep/prune, and dup-cluster consolidation all require the judge, which is off. Observed live on the warm ls20 run: eagerJudge queue = 69 items, judgedClusters = 0, zero verdicts, zero superseded notes; the gated contradiction-supersession (ZONOID_CONTRADICTION_RESOLUTION=1) detected/queued but could never adjudicate. Why drains are off in bench: the drain spawns claude -p judge subprocesses that would perturb the controlled single-agent measurement and burn extra usage. Implication: to validate judge-mediated features, run them where drains are ON (main daemon) OR run a one-shot judge drain against the bench daemon after the run OR add a judge-on bench variant. SEPARATE design point surfaced same run: contradiction supersession is correct for a stale-vs-current FACT (marker moved) but WRONG for competing UNVERIFIED hypotheses (ls20 avatar-dock vs top-box win theory, neither scored) — auto-superseding could retire the correct one; keep both until evidence (a score) decides.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-28T15:42:27.314Z","vec":[-0.03905272111296654,0.02039867453277111,-0.05758970230817795,0.032707858830690384,0.04821706563234329,0.012131555937230587,0.0007244417211040854,0.06247563287615776,0.024970130994915962,0.06994649022817612,-0.012895606458187103,0.026642967015504837,0.04242971912026405,-0.025841835886240005,-0.035956576466560364,0.014872354455292225,0.12988105416297913,-0.0562141016125679,-0.025369353592395782,-0.007170776836574078,0.05065566301345825,-0.0345939621329307